Also proprietary: the surveyLanderAppearance artwork definition only in
modules/appearance-trainer/src/index.ts, as marked by scoped source notices.
The module API, trainerAppearance, trainerArtwork and remaining module code
remain MIT; see modules/appearance-trainer/LICENSE.

The proprietary scope includes Space Sim Classic and Space Sim Tiles Demo,
their game content and assets, the listed tile-demo implementations, and
generated game content derived from these proprietary sources. Its terms
are reproduced below and in LICENSE-GAME.txt inside each game directory.
SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Project in these game files refers to
these proprietary terms, not to the engine MIT license.

All remaining first-party files retain their existing MIT licensing,
including games/space-sim-nextgen (deprecated), other example games,
shared hosts and build tools. Shared code and public APIs used by a game
remain MIT; their inclusion does not make the proprietary game MIT.
Third-party components retain their respective licenses and notices;
see CREDITS.md and bundled notices such as NODE-LICENSE.txt.

